          "year": 1997,
          "date_decided": "1997-03-28",
          "holding": "Termination was affirmed: an ADA noncompliance claim is not a defense to a termination petition because the ADA does not directly apply to such proceedings, and a stipulation limiting SRS's recommendations had no greater force than a judgment and was modifiable on changed circumstances.",
          "relevance": "The written agreement placing mother and child together at a family center is the paradigm of a voluntary service arrangement, and B.S. defines its legal weight.",
          "quote": "We conclude that the ADA does not directly apply to TPR proceedings.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/8209505/in-re-bs/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 8209505
        },
